Refuse to run `upki fetch` as root.

Fetching as root would leave root-owned files in the revocation cache that the
unprivileged fetch service can then no longer update.

Ported to v1.0.1 from Ubuntu's refuse-fetch-as-root.patch by Julian Andres
Klode <julian.klode@canonical.com>, https://git.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/upki

